# Project Rules — .project-rules

## Tech Stack
- Framework: Next.js 16 / React 19 / Node 22
- Language: TypeScript (strict)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS 4 + shadcn/ui
- Database: Drizzle ORM + MySQL
- API: tRPC + Express
- Auth: OAuth2 + JWT (HttpOnly cookies)
- State: TanStack Query (server) + Zustand (client)
- Testing: Vitest + Playwright
- Deploy: Vercel + GitHub Actions

## Coding Standards
- File naming: kebab-case for routes, PascalCase for components
- Import order: React → External → Internal → Local (enforced by eslint)
- Export style: Named exports preferred over default
- Error handling: TRPCError or HTTP error codes with descriptive messages
- Comments: NONE by default — only add when why cannot be conveyed through naming/structure

## Architecture Conventions
- Feature-Sliced Design: app/ → processes/ → features/ → entities/ → shared/
- Colocation: Co-locate related files together in route segments
- Private folders: Prefix non-routable folders with `_` (e.g., `_components`, `_lib`)
- Route groups: Use `(group)` naming for layout partitioning without URL impact
- Server Components: By default everything is Server Component, `'use client'` ONLY at leaf level
- Data fetching: `async/await` directly in Server Components, no useEffect pattern needed
- State Management split: TanStack Query for server state, Zustand for client global, URL params for routing state
- NEVER mix server state and client state — causes double-fetching and stale cache

## Testing Requirements
- Unit tests: Vitest for pure functions, hooks, utils — ~80%+ coverage
- Integration tests: Vitest for tRPC routers, DB queries with test database
- E2E tests: Playwright for critical user journeys only (5-10% of total tests)
- Never chase 100% coverage — it's a quality indicator not a goal
- Follow Kent C. Dodds principles: test behavior, not implementation details

## Git Workflow
- Branch strategy: Trunk-Based Development (short-lived feature branches <24h turnaround)
- Commit format: Conventional Commits (`feat(auth): add OAuth flow`, `fix(api): resolve race condition`)
- PR process: Draft PR → CI checks pass → Review → Approve → Merge → Auto-delete branch
- Always run `pnpm build && pnpm test` before pushing to main

## Security Checklist
- Never hardcode secrets (use `.env` files excluded from version control)
- Validate all user input with Zod schemas before processing
- Rate limit auth endpoints (`express-rate-limit` middleware)
- Use HttpOnly cookies for JWT tokens (not localStorage)
- Enforce CSP headers via Helmet.js
- CORS restricted to explicit origins only (never `*` in production)
- Parameterized SQL queries exclusively (Drizzle handles this automatically)
- HTTPS enforced in production
